  "id": "shirei_eretz_yisrael",
  "name": "Shirei Eretz Yisrael (Hebrew songs of the Land of Israel)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Hebrew-language song repertoire created from the 1920s through the 1950s in the Jewish settlements of Mandate Palestine and early Israel, much of it written by composers such as Mordechai Zeira, Nahum Nardi and Yedidya Admon for the pioneer (halutz) movement, kibbutz festivals, youth movements and shira b'tzibur community-singing evenings. Its melodies drew on Eastern European Jewish and Russian song, hora dance tunes and Yemenite and Arab modal inflections, and the songs spread through songbooks, radio and accordion-led group singing before Hed Arzi and Kol Israel recordings fixed many of them on disc.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-1920s shirei eretz yisrael, ballad Poetry. solo with instrumental accompaniment. accordion, grand piano, parlor acoustic guitar. hardwood living. RCA 44-BX, calrec BBC-broadcast pre, BBC broadcast console, Telefunken u73b broadcast comp, broadcast loudness EQ. AM-radio broadcast.",
